                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "8\\times6!=5760",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p9-q22-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Choose Bob’s seat; Mary’s seat is then fixed. Arrange the five friends and the empty seat.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Bob has 8 seat choices, and Mary must take the seat directly opposite him. Arrange the five friends and the empty seat in the remaining six positions.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=8\\times1\\times6!\\\\N&=5760.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q22-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Bob and Mary sit on the same side, with exactly one seat between them (whether occupied or empty).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p9-q22-c-short-one-seat",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "8\\times6!=5760",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p9-q22-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Choose the side, one of two seat pairs and Bob and Mary’s order. Arrange the five friends and the empty seat.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Number the seats on each side from 1 to 4. The pairs with exactly one intervening seat are $(1,3)$ and $(2,4)$. Choose the side, choose the pair, and choose Bob and Mary’s order. Arrange the five friends and the empty seat in the remaining six positions.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=2\\times2\\times2!\\times6!\\\\N&=5760.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q22-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Bob and Mary sit on opposite sides, and are not directly opposite each other.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p9-q22-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "8\\times3\\times6!=17\\,280",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p9-q22-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bob has 8 seat choices and Mary has 3 permitted seats. Arrange the remaining five people and the empty seat.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Bob has 8 seat choices. Of the four seats on the other side, Mary may take any except the seat directly opposite Bob, giving 3 choices. Arrange the five friends and the empty seat in the remaining six positions.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=8\\times3\\times6!\\\\N&=17\\,280.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
